   587	We close this section applying the formula of Theorem \ref{Theorem 5.6} to two graphs.
   588	
   589	\begin{example}
   590	(i) Consider the $3$-cliques $K(1)=\left(\{1,2,3\}, \{\{1,2\},\{1,3\},\{2,3\}\}\right)$, $K(2)=\left(\{3,4,5\}, \{\{3,4\},\{3,5\},\{4,5\}\}\right)$, and $K(3)=\left(\{1,5,6\}, \{\{1,5\},\{1,6\},\{5,6\}\}\right)$. Let $G=K(1)\cup K(2)\cup K(3)$. 
