The first adversary run found a real failure: degree-ordered greedy maximal independent set recovered a valid side on 5 of 8 shipping instances, so G6 correctly failed. I’m hardening the distribution with a symmetric two-vertex bait—one bait on each true side, nonadjacent to each other, and equally high-degree—so the greedy rule commits to both sides without creating a one-sided plant signature. I’m also removing avoidable work from the 200k-guess measurement.
